OL,3,GNEWSAPlans confirmed to reopen Glens of
OL,4,AAntrim Potato crisp factory
OL,5,
OL,6,FA Northern Ireland crisp brand are set
OL,7,Fto return to supermarket shelves after
OL,8,Fa family-run food producer announced
OL,9,Fplans to restart production.
OL,11,FMilgro, which is based in Limavady and
OL,12,Fis best known for its crispy onion
OL,13,Fproducts, said it had acquired the
OL,14,FGlens of Antrim Crisps brand and
OL,15,Fplanned to reopen the factory in
OL,16,FCushendall, County Antrim.
OL,18,FThe factory employed 43 people when its
OL,19,Fprevious owner, Glens of Antrim
OL,20,FPotatoes, went into administration in
OL,21,FSeptember.
OL,23,APub: 16-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
